      "note": "Release results from paper Table 2. All numbers are pass@1 (percentage of scenarios passing the ARE Verifier on a single run), reported per capability split and averaged over 3 runs per scenario. Scaffold is the paper's ReAct-style harness at temperature 0.5 with 16K tokens/turn and a 200-step cap; the same scaffold is used for every model. Headline: GPT-5 (high) tops the benchmark at 42.1% overall, Claude-4-Sonnet is the best non-reasoning model at 34.8%, Kimi-K2 is the strongest open model at 20.1%. Frontier reasoning models score near-zero on the Time split because inference latency violates temporal tolerances — an 'inverse scaling' phenomenon documented in paper section 4.3."
    },
