  "notes": "GAIA2 (Froger et al., Meta, 2025; arXiv:2509.17158) is an agentic benchmark built on Meta's ARE (Agents Research Environments) platform. ARE simulates a Mobile smartphone with 10 distinct 'universes' and 101 tools covering email, messaging, calendar, contacts, shopping, and similar surfaces. The core release is 800 unique human-annotated scenarios (5 core capability splits of 160 scenarios each: Execution, Search, Ambiguity, Adaptability, Time). Noise (160) and Agent2Agent (160) augmentations, derived from the 160-scenario Gaia2-mini subset, bring the full set to 1,120 evaluation instances across seven capability dimensions.\n\nThe primary metric is pass@1. Pass/fail on each scenario is decided by the ARE Verifier, a rubric-based LLM judge running Llama 3.3 70B Instruct at temperature 0. Each scenario is run 3 times, and the final number is macro-averaged across splits. ARE is asynchronous: environment time advances independently of the agent, which exposes latency-sensitive failure modes invisible in static benchmarks.\n\nResults cover the original 2025-09 paper, the 2026-02 ICLR camera-ready (3 added reasoning-mode variants, same scaffold), and the current live Gaia2-CLI leaderboard (2026-04-14, different 'OpenClaw' scaffold, 5-split overall only). Paper-overall and leaderboard-overall are named differently in the metric column so they are not silently averaged together."
